* If the pickup is a coin, it also has a 20% chance to be replaced with a {{E|Fly}}.

== Notes ==
* All items, trinkets, cards, machines, etc. that spawn coins and keys synergize with this trinket and will cause a random pickup to be spawned instead.
* The floors during the [[Ascent]] are unaffected.
* This trinket has no effect in [[Greed Mode]].
* Coins and keys generated prior to holding Nuh Uh! are unaffected.

== Synergies ==
'''*Any mention of "Random pickups" refers to the above table.  ''"~#"'' are averages as 20% of coins are flies.'''
* {{A|Golden Trinket|r+}} / {{I|Mom's Box|r+}}: Each copy grants +10% chance to spawn the double variant of pickups.
* {{I|Head of the Keeper}}: Coins generated by Head of the Keeper will be replaced with random pickups.
* {{I|Sanguine Bond}}: 17% of the time, generates ''~5'' random pickups, often allowing infinite use with red hearts.
* The {{R|Sacrifice Room}} will pay out with ''~26'' random pickups on it's 10th use 50% of the time.
* {{I|Midas' Touch}} / {{I|Eye of Greed}}: Enemies affected by Midas' touch will drop 1-4 random pickups.
** Because 20% of coins become harmless {{E|Fly|text=flies}}, 20% of the time you can trigger this effect again by affecting and killing spawned flies.
* {{I|Wooden Nickel}}: Can generate a random pickup ''~40%'' of the time.
** {{I|4.5 Volt}}: Generate random pickups over the course of a fight.
* {{I|Blank Card}}: Allows repeated use of card effects that synergize with this trinket.
** {{P|IX - The Hermit?}}: Pickups / Items are sold and turned into other random pickups.
** {{P|XIV - Temperance}}: The generated machine now drops random pickups.
** {{P|Ace of Diamonds}} / {{P|Ace of Spades}}: Re-rolls pickups in the room into other random pickups or turns enemies into random pickups.
** {{P|XII - The Hanged Man?}}: Slain enemies drop random pickups.
** {{P|A Card Against Humanity}}: Coins dropped by generated poops become random pickups.
*** {{I|Midas' Touch}} / {{T|Petrified Poop}}: Greatly increases the amount of coins and thus the amount of random pickups.
* {{P|Soul of the Keeper}}: Creates ''0-25'' random pickups.
* {{I|IV Bag}} / {{I|Piggy Bank}} / {{T|Swallowed Penny}}: Convert health into random pickups.
** {{I|Gimpy}} / {{I|Old Bandage}} / {{I|Fanny Pack}}: Further increase the chance of hearts appearing after use allowing the generation of even more random pickups.
* {{C|Tainted Keeper}}: Coins generated by killing enemies will be replaced by random pickups, however they will still disappear after a short time.
* {{T|Lucky Rock}}: ''26.6%'' of rocks exploded will drop random pickups.
* {{I|Guppy's Tail}}: The keys needed to open gold chests will be converted to other pickups. However, the large quantities of coins generated from chests can be turned into many random pickups. Dropping Nuh Uh! at the start of the floor and then picking it back up to collect random pickups later allows for keys to collected but still gain large quantities of random pickups. Due to the large amount of pills and bombs generated, having the Bombs are Key [[pill]] effect in the pool may allow you to turn a surplus of bombs into a surplus of keys as needed.

== Interactions ==
* {{A|Golden Trinket}} / {{i|Mom's Box}}: No effect.
* Unless dropped or used on pickups spawned prior:
** {{T|Blessed Penny}} / {{T|Charged Penny}} and other penny trinkets can no longer be used.
** {{I|Bumbo}} / {{I|Bum Friend}} / {{I|Key Bum}}: No longer function except for associated [[transformations]]. ({{tf|Super Bum}})
** {{I|Sharp Key}}: Can no longer pickup keys to use.
** {{C|Keeper}} and{{C|Tainted Keeper}} can no longer pickup coins to heal.

